.TH HELIOS 1 "2026-09-21" "Helios Agent 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
helios \- bounded provider-neutral coding agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B helios
[OPTIONS] [PROMPT]
.br
.B helios exec
[OPTIONS] PROMPT
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bare
.B helios
opens the interactive TTY session. Use
.B exec
for non-interactive automation. Provider credentials are resolved from the
OS keyring or the provider-specific environment fallback; values are never
printed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --workspace PATH
Use the canonical workspace PATH.
.TP
.B --provider NAME
Select fake, OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, or a generic OpenAI-compatible provider.
.TP
.B --output-format FORMAT
For exec, select text, json, or stream-json.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR helios (1),
.BR agent-cli (1)
.SH LOCAL COMMANDS
.B helios resume
opens a workspace-scoped resumed TTY session.  
.B helios models --json
lists local provider capability metadata without network access.  
.B helios review security|performance|tests --json
reads the current bounded worktree diff and emits a read-only review envelope.
